    "title": "Sioux City hospital receives Level 3 NICU designation - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By TIM SEAMAN Maren Ewertz ,\n1 hours ago SIOUX CITY , Iowa ( KCAU ) — Already known for its advanced maternal and newborn care, UnityPoint Health St. Luke’s is now designated as having a Level 3 neonatal intensive care unit (NICU).\nHospital officials said the status strengthens St. Luke’s ability to care for infants with complex medical needs.\nStory continues below\nAccording to a press release from St. Luke’s, a Level 3 NICU is equipped to care for newborns of premature gestational age, including infants born earlier than 32 weeks and those requiring advanced respiratory support, continuous monitoring, and complex medical interventions.\nSt. Luke’s cares for nearly 400 NICU babies a year, according to the hospital, with approximately 2,000 babies born each year.\nUnityPoint St. Luke’s is Sioux City’s only hospital after acquiring MercyOne Siouxland in 2025.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to KCAU 9 News | Sioux City, IA | News, Weather, and Sports.",
